    "description": "Catalyst Old River Hydroelectric owns the Sidney A. Murray Jr. Hydroelectric Station on the Mississippi River near Vidalia, Louisiana. The asset serves utility and municipal offtakers through an asset-heavy hydro generation model supported by long-duration contractual arrangements. Public financing materials describe the facility as a 192 MW hydro plant with power sales to an Entergy subsidiary and the Town of Vidalia through contracts extending to 2031. The project is a long-life essential power asset rather than a diversified development platform, and reviewed sources do not disclose a separate project-company founding year. ArcLight has identified Catalyst Old River as a current investment, while public sources do not disclose the current ownership percentages at the asset level.",
